%% NOTE (aspirational, not present in code): an earlier draft of this diagram described a unified `Finding(group, key, state, label, detail, evidence, remedy, blocking, elapsed_ms)` record and a `DetectionReport` with a sha256 canonical-JSON digest, fed by six named groups (environment/gateway/credentials/harnesses/integrations/config) through one `detect.run()` engine. Grepping `class Finding`, `DetectionReport`, and `detect.run(` across verdict/ found no such module or shared type. What exists today is the scattered set of dataclasses shown above (DetectionResult, GatewayCandidate, per-harness StatusReport), called directly and separately by cmd_detect/cmd_doctor. Treat the unified Finding/DetectionReport model as a design proposal, not current code.

